# doc.cosm — the parts of the document that are not nodes. Rendered by the deck and the pack; nothing here is in the model proper.

reading:
  draft: "Public sample, draft 0"
  date: 2026-10-18
  author: "comprise-sample"
  mode: "research (public sources only, in one working day); affect and mattering are the modeller's reading and carry a confidence of 0.5 unless stated"
  perspective: "The firm is the Wikimedia Foundation, Inc. The Wikimedia Endowment is its own organization, bonded to it; affiliates, Wikimedia Deutschland, Enterprise partners and the hosting donors are counterparties. No person is named: seats are roles."
  note: "Facts change: the newest source wins and every figure carries its fiscal year (1 July to 30 June). Audited and Form 990 totals differ a little (2024-25 revenue $208.6M audited, $205.4M on the Form 990)."

history:
  - {date: 2026-07-16, event: "The Foundation explains why large reusers should come through Wikimedia Enterprise and says it will not switch off public API access", sources: ["https://wikimediafoundation.org/news/2026/07/16/wikimedia-enterprise-protecting-wikipedia-ai/"]}
  - {date: 2026-01-15, event: "Wikipedia's 25th birthday: Amazon, Meta, Microsoft, Mistral AI and Perplexity named among Wikimedia Enterprise partners", sources: ["https://enterprise.wikimedia.com/blog/wikipedia-25-enterprise-partners/", "https://wikimediafoundation.org/news/2026/01/15/wikipedia-celebrates-25years/"]}
  - {date: 2025-10-17, event: "The Foundation reports human page views down about 8% against 2024 and names generative AI and social video", sources: ["https://diff.wikimedia.org/2025/10/17/new-user-trends-on-wikipedia/"]}
  - {date: 2023-09-30, event: "The Wikimedia Endowment starts as a standalone 501(c)(3) with its own Board", sources: ["https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/foundation/3/3f/Wikimedia_Foundation_FY_24-25_Audit_Report.pdf", "https://wikimediaendowment.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Wikimedia-Endowment-Audit-Report-FY-24-25.pdf"]}
  - {date: 2022-06-21, event: "Google and the Internet Archive named as the first Wikimedia Enterprise customers", sources: ["https://wikimediafoundation.org/news/2022/06/21/wikimedia-enterprise-announces-google-and-internet-archive-first-customers/"]}
  - {date: 2021-10-25, event: "Wikimedia Enterprise launches", sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Enterprise", "https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Memory:Timeline"]}
  - {date: 2020, event: "The Board is expanded to up to 16 Trustees", sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Memory:Timeline"]}
  - {date: 2016-01, event: "Creation of the Wikimedia Endowment announced, run at first as a donor-advised fund at the Tides Foundation", sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Memory:Timeline"]}
  - {date: 2008-01-31, event: "The move of the headquarters from Florida to San Francisco is complete", sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Memory:Timeline"]}
  - {date: 2003-06-20, event: "The Wikimedia Foundation is founded in Florida", sources: ["https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Memory:Timeline"]}

findings:
  - check: "flow fit · dependency"
    nodes: [P:service/donation-campaigns, P:offering/wikipedia, M:audience/readers]
    finding: "Banner appeals brought $62.4M, 30% of 2024-25 revenue, and they depend on people arriving at the site; the Foundation itself reports human page views down about 8% in recent months of 2025 against 2024."
    proposal: "The 2026-27 plan's goals (reach beyond search, repeat readers and donors, apps) are aimed at this; track banner revenue against human page views in the same quarter."
  - check: "evidence · two bases"
    nodes: [C:finance/2024-07-to-2025-06, C:filing/form-990-2024]
    finding: "The audited statements show revenue of $208.6M and expenses of $190.9M for 2024-25, the Form 990 $205.4M and $189.7M; the Foundation does not reconcile them on the pages read."
    proposal: "Ask for the reconciliation, and keep both in the model, as here; the pages read do not explain the difference."
  - check: "bond · two sides disagree"
    nodes: [C:bond/foundation-manages-endowment, C:contract/cost-sharing]
    finding: "The Foundation recognised $2,066,234 of cost-sharing revenue in 2024-25 and the Endowment reports $1,466,361 paid, each describing the arrangement in its own words and for its own period."
    proposal: "Ask what each figure counts (period, staff time, direct costs paid and reimbursed) before summing anything across the two atoms."
  - check: "rules · cap"
    nodes: [C:policy/enterprise-revenue-cap, P:offering/wikimedia-enterprise]
    finding: "Enterprise income is capped at 30% of total revenue and was about 4% in 2024-25 ($8.3M), up from $3.4M; the growth the plan wants is far under the cap."
    proposal: "None needed now; the cap is the control to watch if Enterprise becomes the answer to falling traffic."
  - check: "role coverage · evidence gap"
    nodes: [O:chart/foundation, O:position/board-of-trustees]
    finding: "The public pages list titles and departments but not reporting lines or the executive team's decision rights, and the Board's current size is stated two ways (12 seats in the composition, 10 in the member table)."
    proposal: "Confirm with the Foundation if this sample is ever claimed; until then these stay pending."

